Live position: watchPosition, accuracy halo, zone readout

The locate button was a one-shot getCurrentPosition that failed silently.
It now holds a watch, draws your position with a halo sized to the reported
accuracy, and follows you until you pan the map by hand.

A "Where you are" panel shows the zone you are standing in, whether duck
season is open there today, the fix age and accuracy, and warns when a
closed area is within two miles. Sunrise, sunset and tides recompute for
your position rather than the map centre.

Failures are now visible and specific: denied, no fix, or timed out, with
different advice depending on whether the page is embedded in a frame.

